{#- Expects `interface` in scope; rendered after the switchport lines. `interface.mlag_id` is the lag_id of a
    host-facing port-channel of a vPC pair (transforms/helpers/vxlan.py), the same on both peers; it is never set
    on the peer-link, which carries `vpc peer-link` (cisco_nxos_vpc.j2).
    documented-not-lab-verified: Cisco Nexus 9000 Series NX-OS Layer 2 Switching Configuration Guide, "Configuring
    vPCs": `vpc <number>` under `interface port-channel <n>`, the same number on both vPC peers, on a Layer 2
    (switchport) port-channel. The section text was NOT opened (the Cisco page returned 404 when this was written);
    only the Arista side is quoted from its manual (arista_eos_mlag_id.j2). Confirm against the Cisco guide.
    A virtual peer-link renders no vPC domain (cisco_nxos_vpc.j2), and `vpc <id>` needs the domain. -#}
{%- if interface.mlag_id is defined and interface.vlans and not (mlag and mlag.virtual_peer_link) %}
  vpc {{ interface.mlag_id }}
{%- endif -%}
